(* SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later *)
(* formal/hx.pv — SecMP-HX (docs/03 §6) with SecMP-INV (§5.4, §5.5) and the first SecMP-TR cell (§7.2–§7.4) as
   used by the handshake. Query set: formal/CLAIMS.md §HX (H1–H12c, fixed by the reviewer; ADR-026, docs/03 §11.2).
   Properties: docs/03 §11.1 row "HX". Run: proverif formal/hx.pv (ProVerif 2.05).

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1. What is modelled (CLAIMS §HX "Model")
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   An honest responder R (the inviter) and an honest initiator I (the invitee) per session (3.).
   R: IKS_R = (IK_sig_R, IK_dh_R), one signed-prekey generation (SPK_dh_R, SPK_kem_R, RPK_kem_R), published IKSPublic_R.
   Per issued invitation (replicated): a fresh OPK_j = (OPK_dh_R[j], OPK_kem_R[j]) with opk_id_j, a fresh ld_id_j
   (relay-visible: output on c) and link_key_j; R signs the bundle (§6.3: HybridSign(IK_sig, "SecMP-HX/1 bundle",
   all preceding fields ‖ ik_dh)) — event BundleSigned — and issues the invitation — event InvIssued; the
   InvitationV1_j (ld_id, link_key, inviter_fp = fingerprint(IKS_R), §5.2; the queue fields inv_sid/inv_send_seed
   carry no HX key material and are not modelled) goes to I on the private out-of-band channel pinv(s) (published on
   c under LeakInv); the link-data blob N ‖ CAEAD.Seal(K_ld, N, "SecMP-INV/1 blob" ‖ ld_id, LinkDataV1(IKS_R,
   bundle, Profile_R, created)) (§5.4) is output on c. The attacker is Dolev–Yao on c and is the relay: any cell
   may be delivered, dropped, replayed or injected.
   I (replicated): takes an invitation (from pinv(s); in every session except hId* also from c: the attacker as
   inviter), takes a blob from c, performs §5.5 steps 2–4 (open under K_ld; fingerprint(inviter_iks) = inviter_fp;
   bundle signature under inviter_iks.IK_sig and opk_present = 0x01; expiry checks are not modelled: no time), then
   §6.4 with a fresh EK_I and fresh Encaps randomness: DH1 = X25519(IK_dh_I, SPK_dh_R), DH2 = X25519(EK_I, IK_dh_R),
   DH3 = X25519(EK_I, SPK_dh_R), DH4 = X25519(EK_I, OPK_dh_R), (ct_spk, ss_spk), (ct_opk, ss_opk), transcript (13
   components, `docs/03:313-316`), SK, K_id; §7.2 initiator initialisation and §7.3 Encrypt of the Content
   Handshake(Profile_I, caps = 0, routes_I) (§7.6) = first_msg; §6.5 Inner = IKSPublic_I ‖ first_msg, inner_ct
   under K_id ("SecMP-HX/1 inner" ‖ ld_id), Outer = EK_I ‖ spk_id ‖ opk_id ‖ ct_spk ‖ ct_opk ‖ inner_ct (ver is a
   constant, omitted), three chunks sealed under K_inv ("SecMP-HX/1 initcell" ‖ ld_id) with init_id, i, total.
   Event IStart, then the three cells are output on c. EK_I is never output and is not part of any later reveal
   (discarded after IStart, ADR-044 (b)). I then waits for R's first TR reply (H6b): §7.4 step path under nhk_r =
   NHK_B, new-ratchet-key check (dh_pk ≠ SPK_dh_R), DHRatchet receiving half, KDF_CK, MsgDecrypt — event IConfirm.
   R (replicated acceptance attempts per invitation): takes three cells from c, reads the invitation's single-use
   OPK cell (6.), performs §6.6 steps 1–3: open the chunks under K_inv (same init_id, i = 0, 1, 2, total = 3),
   join, parse Outer, spk_id/opk_id = this invitation's ids (step 1); DH3, DH4, ss_spk, ss_opk, K_id, open inner_ct
   → IKSPublic_I (decodable: an iks(vk, G) term) and first_msg (step 2); DH1, DH2, transcript, SK, §7.2 responder
   initialisation (dh_s = SPK_dh_R, kem_s = RPK_kem_R, nhk_r = HK_A), first_msg on the §7.4 step path (header under
   HK_A, n = 0, pn = 0, ADR-044 (e); DHRatchet receiving half with Decaps(RPK_kem_R, ct_pq) and X25519(SPK_dh_R,
   dh_pk); KDF_CK; MsgDecrypt; Content type Handshake) (step 3). Any failure re-outputs the OPK cell (step 3 "keep
   the OPK"); on success event RAccept, the OPK cell is not re-output (step 4 "delete the OPK"), and R sends its
   first TR reply (DHRatchet sending half with fresh keys, §7.3 under hk_s = NHK_B) on c.
   Paths covered / excluded: CLAIMS §HX "Paths the model covers / excludes" (referenced, not repeated here).

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2. Abstractions (exactly those of CLAIMS §HX; nothing else about a primitive is assumed)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     X25519               exp with exp(exp(g,a),b) = exp(exp(g,b),a); the all-zero check is not modelled (test)  §3
     ML-KEM-1024          pk1024/encaps_ct1024/encaps_ss1024, decaps1024(dk, encaps_ct1024(pk1024(dk), r)) =
                          encaps_ss1024(pk1024(dk), r) (SPK_kem, OPK_kem; implicit rejection not modelled)      §3
     ML-KEM-768           pk768/encaps_ct768/encaps_ss768/decaps768 (RPK_kem, TR first step), as §TR            §3
     h(x)                 SHA-256, public one-way; fp(iks) = h(("SecMP-FP/1", iks))                         §6.2
     th(13 args)          the §6.4 transcript, a free public constructor                                       §6.4
     hx_sk, hx_kid        SK = hx_sk(DH1, DH2, DH3, DH4, ss_spk, ss_opk, th); K_id = hx_kid(ld_id, link_key, DH3,
                          ss_spk, DH4, ss_opk) (DH1, DH2 not inputs); salt/prefix constants omitted              §6.4
     hx_kinv, inv_kld     K_inv = hx_kinv(ld_id, link_key) §6.5; K_ld = inv_kld(ld_id, link_key) §5.4
     caead_seal/open      CAEAD (§3.4), AD checked, committing (blob, the three cells, inner_ct)
     chunk0/1/2, join     join(chunk0(x), chunk1(x), chunk2(x)) = x; pad is the identity                      §6.5
     hsign/hverify        HybridSign as one unforgeable signature; hverify(vk(sk), l, m, hsign(sk, l, m)) = true §3.5
     hkdf_init, kdf_rk, kdf_ck, hseal/hopen, bseal/bopen   exactly as §TR (formal/tr.pv §2; hseal2 is T12-only and
                          not used here)                                                                 §7.2–§7.4
     IKSPublic = iks(vk(IK_sig), exp(g, IK_dh)) (a data constructor); PrekeyBundle = the §6.3 field tuple; constant
     ver fields omitted; spk_expiry, opk_present, Profile_R, created, Profile_I are public constants.
   Honest secrets are private constructors applied to (session tag, index): dhsk(s, k) = X25519 secrets, kemsk(s, k)
   = ML-KEM decapsulation keys, kemr(s, k) = Encaps randomness, iksig(s, P) = IK_sig. Fixed indices name the
   long-term keys (kIKR, kIKI, kSPK, kRPK); per-invitation and per-I-session keys use a fresh name as index (new o;
   dhsk(s, o)), so every honest secret of session s has the form dhsk(s, _), kemsk(s, _), kemr(s, _) or iksig(s, _).

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3. Sessions (the claims' scenarios run as independent parallel sessions of one process)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     tag          inv. from c  PubIKS  LeakInv  RevealLT(R)  RevealLT(I)  RevealSPK  RevealOPK  DHO   KEMO   queries
     hClean       yes          yes     ph 0     -            -            -          -          -     -      H1, H5, H6b, H10
     hDH          yes          yes     ph 0     -            -            -          -          ph 0  -      H2, H8
     hKEM         yes          yes     ph 0     -            -            -          -          -     ph 0   H3, H5
     hBoth        yes          yes     ph 0     -            -            -          -          ph 0  ph 0   H4
     hId          -            -       -        -            -            -          -          -     -      H7a
     hIdThief     -            -       ph 0     -            -            -          -          -     -      H7b
     hIdLater     -            -       ph 1     ph 1         -            ph 1       -          ph 1  -      H7c
     hIdLaterOPK  -            -       ph 1     ph 1         -            ph 1       ph 1       ph 1  -      H7d
     hKCI         yes          yes     ph 0     -            -            ph 0       -          -     -      H9
     hKCIlt       yes          yes     ph 0     ph 0         -            -          -          -     -      H9b
     hKCIi        yes          yes     ph 0     -            ph 0         -          -          -     -      H9c
     hFS          yes          yes     ph 1     ph 1         ph 1         ph 1       -          -     -      H12
     hFSOPK       yes          yes     ph 1     ph 1         ph 1         ph 1       ph 1       -     -      H12b
     hFSDH        yes          yes     ph 1     ph 1         ph 1         ph 1       -          ph 1  -      H12c
   plus H6a in every session except hKCIlt (RevealLT(R) before IStart) and H11 in every session. hKCIi's row in
   CLAIMS names no invitation leak; LeakInv ph 0 is added (H9c is H1 (i), whose assumptions include it; it only
   strengthens the attacker). "inv. from c": I also takes invitations from c (the attacker as inviter with its own
   identity); in hId* sessions I runs only on R's invitation and IKS_I is never output in clear. In every session
   the attacker may send R envelopes under its own identity (R reads cells from c). Sessions share no private
   value: every secret is a private constructor applied to the session's tag, and the private channels are per tag
   (pinv(s)) or fresh (the OPK cells). The only shared symbols are public (g, labels, constants, tags) and the oracle
   destructors, which are scoped per session (4.). Hence removing the other sessions from the process only removes
   attacker capabilities, so a query proved true here also holds in a model that contains its scenario alone; the
   attacks reported for the false queries were checked to use only their own session (report §3).
   Events carry the session tag as first argument; every query names its tag.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   4. Oracles, "enabled per query" and scoped per session as formal/tr.pv §4
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   DHO:  dh_break(exp(g, dhsk(s,x)), exp(g, dhsk(s,y))) = exp(exp(g, dhsk(s,x)), dhsk(s,y)) — every pair of honest
         X25519 exponents of session s (IK_dh_I, IK_dh_R, SPK_dh_R, OPK_dh_R[j], EK_I, the TR initiator's dh_s, R's
         reply dh_s). Phase 0 (public destructor dh_break): hDH, hBoth. Phase 1 (private destructor dh_break1,
         offered by the process DHO1 from phase 1 on): hIdLater, hIdLaterOPK, hFSDH.
   KEMO: kem_break1024(encaps_ct1024(ek, kemr(s,r))) = encaps_ss1024(ek, kemr(s,r)) (ct_spk, ct_opk) and
         kem_break768(encaps_ct768(ek, kemr(s,r))) = encaps_ss768(ek, kemr(s,r)) (the ML-KEM-768 encapsulation to
         RPK_kem_R of the TR first step, and R's reply): hKEM, hBoth (phase 0, public).
   Soundness of the scoping as formal/tr.pv §4: every exponent / ciphertext of a session is either honest (of the
   form dhsk(s,_) / encaps_ct(_, kemr(s,_)), covered by the rule) or built by the attacker from values it knows (its
   result computable without the oracle); outside its session the oracle applies to nothing.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   5. Compromise (each emits its event and outputs the values on c, in the phase of the session's row)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     LeakInv(s, ld_id)       InvitationV1 (ld_id, link_key, inviter_fp), per invitation
     RevealLT(s, P)          P's IK_sig and IK_dh secrets
     RevealSPK(s, pR)        SPK_dh_R secret, SPK_kem_R and RPK_kem_R decapsulation keys
     RevealOPK(s, pR, ld_id) OPK_j secrets, per invitation (sanity: "the OPK was not deleted")
     PubIKS(s, pI)           IKSPublic_I in clear
   Phase 1 discards every phase-0 process: R's acceptance attempts, R's and I's sessions end; the queries' attacker
   facts are evaluated at the end of phase 1.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   6. OPK bookkeeping (CLAIMS O-7; M3 R-13)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A single-use private cell per OPK_j: a fresh private channel ocell; R outputs the OPK secrets on it once; every
   acceptance attempt (replicated) reads it after taking the cells, re-outputs it on every failure path of §6.6
   steps 1–3 (the letfun accept13 fails ⇒ else branch) and does not re-output it after step 3 succeeded (RAccept).
   Injectivity of H5/H10 is not obtained from process structure: acceptance attempts, invitations and I sessions are
   all replicated.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   7. Devices (none changes the model's semantics or weakens a query)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   - Each X25519 value is bound once with let and reused (formal/tr.pv §8).
   - §6.6 steps 1–3 are one letfun (accept13); ProVerif inlines it; a failing let inside it makes the call fail.
   - Names carry no message arguments (new n[]): each name depends only on the replication indices above it, not on
     the messages received before it (ProVerif's default embeds them, so the envelope terms nest without bound).
     An over-approximation (names of one session copy are merged across the inputs it could have received; a
     session copy receives each input once), as formal/tr.pv §8.
   - The acceptance attempt reads the OPK cell with the equality patterns (=osk, =odk): the cell only ever holds
     this invitation's OPK (output once by Invitation, re-output unchanged on failure), so the test always succeeds;
     it lets ProVerif bind the OPK in R's clauses instead of carrying it as an unconstrained variable.
   - Ephemeral key indices are eph(fresh name) and long-term ones are constants, so the secrecy assumptions below can
     name them; secrecy assumptions (not attacker(M) [phase 0]) state what a session's row (3.) never reveals;
     ProVerif proves each one and aborts if one cannot be proved ("ok, secrecy assumption verified"), and uses them
     only to discard clauses whose hypotheses can never hold.
   - set selFun = Term (formal/tr.pv §8) and two nounif declarations (the blob and the initcell ciphertexts under
     keys of unbound ld_id/link_key are not selected before the private facts that bind them): resolution strategy,
     termination/performance only.
   - One query declaration, in CLAIMS ID order, a "Hk" comment directly above every query.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   8. Expected verdicts (CLAIMS §HX gate rule), RESULT lines in file order
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   H1 (2) true · H2 (2) true · H3 (2) true · H4 (1) false · H5 (2) true · H6a (13) true · H6b (1) true ·
   H7a (2) true · H7b (2) true · H7c (2) true · H7d (2) false · H8 (1) false · H9 (1) false · H9b (1) true ·
   H9c (1) true · H10 (1) true · H11 (56) false · H12 (2) true · H12b (2) false · H12c (2) true — 98 RESULT lines.
*)

(* ---------------------------------------------------------------- channels, types, constants ------------------ *)

set selFun = Term.

free c: channel.

type key.        (* 32-byte symmetric keys: SK, K_id, K_inv, K_ld, link_key, RK, rk, ck, mk, hk *)
type exponent.   (* X25519 secret *)
type G.          (* X25519 public key / shared secret *)
type kemdk.      (* ML-KEM decapsulation key (seed) *)
type coins.      (* Encaps randomness *)
type nonce.      (* 24-byte nonces *)
type sigsk.      (* IK_sig secret (Ed25519 ‖ ML-DSA-65) *)
type tagt.       (* session (scenario) tag *)

const hClean, hDH, hKEM, hBoth, hId, hIdThief, hIdLater, hIdLaterOPK, hKCI, hKCIlt, hKCIi, hFS, hFSOPK, hFSDH: tagt.
const pR, pI: bitstring.                                  (* parties *)
const kIKR, kIKI, kSPK, kRPK: bitstring.                  (* long-term key indices *)
const yes, no: bitstring.                                 (* session flags *)
const never, ph0, ph1: bitstring.                         (* compromise phase of a session (3.) *)
const lbl_fp, lbl_bundle, lbl_blob, lbl_inner, lbl_initcell, lbl_hdr, lbl_body: bitstring.
      (* "SecMP-FP/1", "SecMP-HX/1 bundle", "SecMP-INV/1 blob", "SecMP-HX/1 inner", "SecMP-HX/1 initcell",
         "SecMP-TR/1 hdr", "SecMP-TR/1 body" (App. A) *)
const spkid0, spkexp0, opk1: bitstring.                   (* spk_id (one generation), spk_expiry, opk_present = 0x01 *)
const profR, created0, profI: bitstring.                  (* Profile_R, created, Profile_I: public *)
const i0, i1, i2, t3: bitstring.                          (* chunk index i = 0, 1, 2; total = 3 *)
const c0: bitstring.                                      (* counter value 0 (n, pn) *)
const ctHS, ctReply: bitstring.                           (* Content type Handshake; R's first reply *)

(* ---------------------------------------------------------------- honest secrets (2.) ------------------------ *)

fun dhsk(tagt, bitstring): exponent [private].            (* X25519.keygen() *)
fun kemsk(tagt, bitstring): kemdk [private].              (* ML-KEM keygen (seed) *)
fun kemr(tagt, bitstring): coins [private].               (* Encaps randomness *)
fun iksig(tagt, bitstring): sigsk [private].              (* IK_sig *)
fun pinv(tagt): channel [private].
fun eph(bitstring): bitstring [data].                     (* index of an ephemeral key *)                        (* out-of-band invitation channel R -> I *)

(* ---------------------------------------------------------------- primitives (CLAIMS abstractions) ----------- *)

(* §3 X25519 *)
const g: G.
fun exp(G, exponent): G.
equation forall x: exponent, y: exponent; exp(exp(g, x), y) = exp(exp(g, y), x).

(* §3 ML-KEM-1024 (SPK_kem, OPK_kem) *)
fun pk1024(kemdk): bitstring.
fun encaps_ct1024(bitstring, coins): bitstring.
fun encaps_ss1024(bitstring, coins): bitstring.
reduc forall dk: kemdk, r: coins; decaps1024(dk, encaps_ct1024(pk1024(dk), r)) = encaps_ss1024(pk1024(dk), r).

(* §3 ML-KEM-768 (RPK_kem; TR) *)
fun pk768(kemdk): bitstring.
fun encaps_ct768(bitstring, coins): bitstring.
fun encaps_ss768(bitstring, coins): bitstring.
reduc forall dk: kemdk, r: coins; decaps768(dk, encaps_ct768(pk768(dk), r)) = encaps_ss768(pk768(dk), r).

(* §6.2 SHA-256, IKSPublic, fingerprint *)
fun h(bitstring): bitstring.
fun iks(bitstring, G): bitstring [data].
letfun fp(x: bitstring) = h((lbl_fp, x)).

(* §6.4 transcript (13 components), SK, K_id; §6.5 K_inv; §5.4 K_ld *)
fun th(bitstring, bitstring, G, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, G, bitstring, bitstring, G, bitstring, bitstring,
       bitstring): bitstring.
fun hx_sk(G, G, G, G, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring): key.
fun hx_kid(bitstring, key, G, bitstring, G, bitstring): key.
fun hx_kinv(bitstring, key): key.
fun inv_kld(bitstring, key): key.

(* §3.4 CAEAD *)
fun caead_seal(key, nonce, bitstring, bitstring): bitstring.
reduc forall k: key, n: nonce, ad: bitstring, m: bitstring; caead_open(k, n, ad, caead_seal(k, n, ad, m)) = m.

(* §6.5 the three 4006-byte chunks of pad(Outer, 12018) *)
fun chunk0(bitstring): bitstring.
fun chunk1(bitstring): bitstring.
fun chunk2(bitstring): bitstring.
reduc forall x: bitstring; join(chunk0(x), chunk1(x), chunk2(x)) = x.

(* §3.5 HybridSign *)
fun vk(sigsk): bitstring.
fun hsign(sigsk, bitstring, bitstring): bitstring.
reduc forall sk: sigsk, l: bitstring, m: bitstring; hverify(vk(sk), l, m, hsign(sk, l, m)) = true.

(* §7.2 hkdf_init(SK) -> (RK, HK_A, NHK_B); KDF_RK; KDF_CK *)
fun init_rk(key): key.
fun init_hka(key): key.
fun init_nhkb(key): key.
fun rk_rk(key, G, bitstring): key.
fun rk_ck(key, G, bitstring): key.
fun rk_nhk(key, G, bitstring): key.
fun ck_ck(key): key.
fun ck_mk(key): key.

(* §7.3 header AEAD; §3.3 MsgEncrypt *)
fun hseal(key, nonce, bitstring, bitstring): bitstring.
reduc forall k: key, n: nonce, ad: bitstring, m: bitstring; hopen(k, n, ad, hseal(k, n, ad, m)) = m.
fun bseal(key, bitstring, bitstring): bitstring.
reduc forall k: key, ad: bitstring, m: bitstring; bopen(k, ad, bseal(k, ad, m)) = m.

(* ---------------------------------------------------------------- oracles (4.) ------------------------------- *)

(* DHO, phase 0: hDH (H2, H8), hBoth (H4) *)
reduc forall x: bitstring, y: bitstring;
        dh_break(exp(g, dhsk(hDH, x)), exp(g, dhsk(hDH, y))) = exp(exp(g, dhsk(hDH, x)), dhsk(hDH, y));
      forall x: bitstring, y: bitstring;
        dh_break(exp(g, dhsk(hBoth, x)), exp(g, dhsk(hBoth, y))) = exp(exp(g, dhsk(hBoth, x)), dhsk(hBoth, y)).

(* DHO, phase 1 only: hIdLater (H7c), hIdLaterOPK (H7d), hFSDH (H12c); private, offered by DHO1 in phase 1 *)
reduc forall x: bitstring, y: bitstring;
        dh_break1(exp(g, dhsk(hIdLater, x)), exp(g, dhsk(hIdLater, y))) =
          exp(exp(g, dhsk(hIdLater, x)), dhsk(hIdLater, y));
      forall x: bitstring, y: bitstring;
        dh_break1(exp(g, dhsk(hIdLaterOPK, x)), exp(g, dhsk(hIdLaterOPK, y))) =
          exp(exp(g, dhsk(hIdLaterOPK, x)), dhsk(hIdLaterOPK, y));
      forall x: bitstring, y: bitstring;
        dh_break1(exp(g, dhsk(hFSDH, x)), exp(g, dhsk(hFSDH, y))) = exp(exp(g, dhsk(hFSDH, x)), dhsk(hFSDH, y))
      [private].

(* KEMO, phase 0: hKEM (H3, H5), hBoth (H4) *)
reduc forall ek: bitstring, r: bitstring;
        kem_break1024(encaps_ct1024(ek, kemr(hKEM, r))) = encaps_ss1024(ek, kemr(hKEM, r));
      forall ek: bitstring, r: bitstring;
        kem_break1024(encaps_ct1024(ek, kemr(hBoth, r))) = encaps_ss1024(ek, kemr(hBoth, r)).
reduc forall ek: bitstring, r: bitstring;
        kem_break768(encaps_ct768(ek, kemr(hKEM, r))) = encaps_ss768(ek, kemr(hKEM, r));
      forall ek: bitstring, r: bitstring;
        kem_break768(encaps_ct768(ek, kemr(hBoth, r))) = encaps_ss768(ek, kemr(hBoth, r)).

(* ---------------------------------------------------------------- events ------------------------------------- *)

event BundleSigned(tagt, bitstring, bitstring).                                   (* (s, iks_R, b) *)
event InvIssued(tagt, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring).                           (* (s, iks_R, ld_id, opk_id) *)
event IStart(tagt, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, key).   (* (s, iks_I, iks_R, b, tr, rt, sk) *)
event RAccept(tagt, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, key).
                                                                  (* (s, iks_R, iks_I, ld_id, opk_id, tr, rt, sk) *)
event IConfirm(tagt, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, key).                       (* (s, iks_I, iks_R, tr, sk) *)
event LeakInv(tagt, bitstring).                                                   (* (s, ld_id) *)
event RevealLT(tagt, bitstring).                                                  (* (s, P) *)
event RevealSPK(tagt, bitstring).                                                 (* (s, pR) *)
event RevealOPK(tagt, bitstring, bitstring).                                      (* (s, pR, ld_id) *)
event PubIKS(tagt, bitstring).                                                    (* (s, pI) *)

(* ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrecy assumptions (7.) -------------------- *)

(* Never output in any session: the invitation channels, the Encaps randomness, the ephemeral keys in phase 0. *)
not s: tagt; attacker(pinv(s)).
not s: tagt, x: bitstring; attacker(kemr(s, x)).
not s: tagt, x: bitstring; attacker(dhsk(s, eph(x))) phase 0.
not s: tagt, x: bitstring; attacker(kemsk(s, eph(x))) phase 0.
(* Per session: the keys its row (3.) never reveals, and those it reveals only in phase 1 (phase 0). *)
not x: bitstring; attacker(dhsk(hClean, eph(x))).
not x: bitstring; attacker(kemsk(hClean, eph(x))).
not attacker(iksig(hClean, pR)).
not attacker(dhsk(hClean, kIKR)).
not attacker(iksig(hClean, pI)).
not attacker(dhsk(hClean, kIKI)).
not attacker(dhsk(hClean, kSPK)).
not attacker(kemsk(hClean, kSPK)).
not attacker(kemsk(hClean, kRPK)).
not x: bitstring; attacker(dhsk(hDH, eph(x))).
not x: bitstring; attacker(kemsk(hDH, eph(x))).
not attacker(iksig(hDH, pR)).
not attacker(dhsk(hDH, kIKR)).
not attacker(iksig(hDH, pI)).
